# Everything is LF, in the index and in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The scaffolds carry their own rule so their LF does not depend on the `*` line above.
# gitattributes is last-match-wins per attribute, so this keeps holding if that line is
# ever narrowed. It matters because most of these are read by Linux tooling once copied
# onto a box (bash, systemd, nginx), where a stray CR is at best noise and at worst fatal.
# If a BINARY `.example` is ever added, exempt it here with `-text`: unlike `text=auto`,
# a forced `text` normalizes regardless of content and would corrupt it.
# NOTE: the `.example` suffix is why `*.ps1` below does NOT match publish-scp.ps1.example.
*.example text eol=lf

# Forward cover for a real .ps1, should one ever land here. Matches nothing today.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
